  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 151 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nSaturday through Wednesday:\n\nBetter model agreement is present today for a wave of WAA and a\nwarm front to bring rain chances (50 to 60% PoPs) during the \nfirst half of Saturday over most of southern WI. Rain chances \nthen look to grow weaker Saturday afternoon (30% PoPs) and \nevening (15% PoPs) as the low to mid level warm advection \nbecomes weaker and the forcing mechanisms for the rain taper \noff.\n\nRain chances then look more nebulous on Sunday as the GFS and\nECMWF show rain over the eastern Corn Belt along a sfc trough \nwhile we remain dry, though these chances are not fair away from\nsouthern WI and may shift with time. As it stands, 15 to 30%\npops are painted across the area for Sunday morning and \nafternoon.\n\nBeyond, the GFS and ECMWF depict a multi-day rain maker \narriving Monday and lingering into Wednesday or Thursday. Exact\ndetails need to be fleshed out but next week looks to remain\nmild and will feature more a more active weather pattern.\n\nCMiller",
